          },
          "blocks": {
            "text_KPqHgz": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "t:names.heading",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>The protein aisle was never built for you.</p>",
                "highlight_style": "none",
                "highlight_font_style": "italic",
                "highlight_shape_color": "",
                "highlight_text_color": "",
                "type_preset": "h1",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_weight": "",
                "font_size": 15,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "line_height": "normal",
                "text_color": "text",
                "text_color_gradient": "",
                "disable_line_break_mobile": false,
                "width": "fit-content",
                "text_alignment": "left",
                "width_mobile": "fit-content",
                "text_alignment_mobile": "left",
                "padding-block-start": 12,
                "padding-block-end": 24,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0,
                "mobile-padding-scale": 79,
                "animation_type": "fade-up",
                "animation_delay": 100
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_3bN7bf": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "t:names.text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Every protein on the shelf was designed for someone chasing a personal record in a gym. The tubs are loud. The scoops are messy. The taste is something you endure because you read somewhere that you need more protein. Then the bloating starts. Then the breakouts. Then the quiet decision to put the tub in the back of the cupboard and forget about it.<br/><br/>That was not your body failing. That was the product failing you. The category was built around a body and a goal that were not yours, and then it blamed you for not finishing the tub.<br/><br/>And even if you did find a protein you could tolerate, you still needed a separate collagen supplement for your skin, a separate enzyme for your digestion, and a separate greens product for anything beyond basic macros. Four products. Four price tags. Four routines. That is not wellness. That is admin.</p>",
                "highlight_style": "none",
                "highlight_font_style": "italic",
                "highlight_shape_color": "",
                "highlight_text_color": "",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_weight": "",
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "line_height": "normal",
                "text_color": "text",
                "text_color_gradient": "",
                "disable_line_break_mobile": false,
                "width": "fit-content",
                "text_alignment": "left",
                "width_mobile": "fit-content",
                "text_alignment_mobile": "left",
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 20,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0,
                "mobile-padding-scale": 75,
                "animation_type": "fade-up",
                "animation_delay": 150
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_bjXhPC": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "t:names.text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><em><strong>You deserve a protein that fits inside your handbag, your morning, and your standards. You deserve it to taste like something you would actually order. You deserve it to do more than one thing. Thrive is what happens when a protein is finally designed with you in the room.</strong></em></p>",
                "highlight_style": "wavy-underline",
                "highlight_font_style": "italic",
                "highlight_shape_color": "#dbd2ef",
                "highlight_text_color": "",
                "type_preset": "paragraph",
