              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_m76FzH": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "text": "Is there research behind this formula?",
                "open_row_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "icon_size": "custom-size",
                "width": 32,
                "width_mobile": 24
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_icCHUc": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes, this took months of research and development. Research suggests women may benefit from more daily protein than traditional guidelines recommend.⁵ The protein in Thrive carries three health claims approved by European food safety authorities: protein contributes to a growth in muscle mass, to the maintenance of muscle mass, and to the maintenance of normal bones. These are not marketing claims. The collagen source has a published absorption study confirming significantly higher bioavailability than standard processing.¹ Every ingredient in the formula was selected to work alongside the protein, not as a marketing add-on. Every reference is listed in the section below.</p>",
                    "highlight_style": "none",
                    "highlight_font_style": "italic",
                    "highlight_shape_color": "",
                    "highlight_text_color": "",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
